<h2 class="font-bold mb-3 text-xl">Euler's Knight Tour</h2>
<p class="mb-1">The Swiss mathematician Leonhard Euler worked out this way of making a knight jump from square to square on a chessboard so that it visits every square just once before returning to its starting point.</p>
<p class="mb-1">This tour has another remarkable property. If the squares are numbered in the order that the knight visits them, the sum of the numbers in every row and every column of the square is 260.</p>